<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Galdan Boshugtu Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1644">1644</a>–<a href="/years/1697">1697</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Galdan Boshugtu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Galdan Boshugtu Khan was ruler of the Dzungar Khanate from 1671 to 1697. A former Buddhist monk trained in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>, he conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yarkent-khanate">Yarkent Khanate</a> in 1680 and invaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalkha-mongols">Khalkha Mongols</a> in 1688. This brought him into war with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kangxi-emperor">Kangxi Emperor</a> of the Qing, who defeated him at Ulan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buton-island">Butung</a> in 1690 and Jao Modo in 1696.</p></div>
